- [ ] **Step 3.3.11: Add styled-vs-plain length test**

This test compares the styled and plain renderings — robust against CI environments where lipgloss's `ColorProfile()` may downgrade. The styled output must be strictly longer than the plain output (because ANSI escapes have to land somewhere) and must contain the literal `●` glyph.

Append:

```go
func TestFormatCheckpointHeader_ColorEnabledRenders(t *testing.T) {
	t.Parallel()

	cpID := id.MustCheckpointID("a3b2c4d5e6f7")
	meta := checkpoint.CommittedMetadata{
		SessionID: "s",
		CreatedAt: time.Date(2026, 4, 29, 14, 22, 8, 0, time.UTC),
	}

	// Force lipgloss to emit ANSI by setting the color profile on a
	// freshly-constructed renderer that the styles use.
	renderer := lipgloss.NewRenderer(io.Discard)
	renderer.SetColorProfile(termenv.TrueColor)

	plainStyles := statusStyles{colorEnabled: false, width: 60}
	colorStyles := statusStyles{
		colorEnabled: true,
		width:        60,
		bold:         renderer.NewStyle().Bold(true),
		dim:          renderer.NewStyle().Faint(true),
		yellow:       renderer.NewStyle().Foreground(lipgloss.Color("3")),
	}

	plain := formatCheckpointHeader(nil, meta, cpID, nil, checkpoint.Author{}, plainStyles)
	styled := formatCheckpointHeader(nil, meta, cpID, nil, checkpoint.Author{}, colorStyles)

	if !strings.Contains(plain, "●") {
		t.Errorf("expected ● glyph in plain output, got:\n%s", plain)
	}
	if !strings.Contains(styled, "●") {
		t.Errorf("expected ● glyph in styled output, got:\n%s", styled)
	}
	if len(styled) <= len(plain) {
		t.Errorf("expected styled length (%d) > plain length (%d) — ANSI escapes should add bytes", len(styled), len(plain))
	}
}
```

The length comparison is robust on CI even though `formatCheckpointHeader` constructs the bullet (`●`) and cpID value with `lipgloss.NewStyle()` (the global renderer, which may emit zero ANSI on a colorless CI profile). The label rendering (`session`, `created`, etc.) goes through `styles.dim` and the tokens row through `styles.yellow` — both come from the **test renderer** wired into `colorStyles` and reliably emit ANSI bytes. So `len(styled) > len(plain)` holds independent of the global renderer's profile.

